Quick answer

Get more reviews without review gating
Some review-request practices are clearly sound. Some are clearly review gating. The difficult decisions sit in the middle and require judgment about customer choice, timing, platform rules, privacy, and the patterns that automated spam systems may see. A business does not have to send a review request after every transaction. It can choose recipients using objective operating rules, avoid asking during an active conflict, offer private recovery, and keep the public-review path available. The strongest programs earn more reviews through timely requests, real personalization, low friction, useful responses, and disciplined measurement.

